Appendix H — Evidence Taxonomy (Formal)

H.1 Levels

Level Epistemic Status Example
E0 Direct user statement "I have been sleeping four hours."
E1 Directly observable behavior Many projects are being developed.
E2 Aggregated behavioral pattern High breadth + high iteration.
E3 Interpretive hypothesis Possible elevated state.
E4 Diagnostic/clinical claim A specific mental-health condition.

H.2 Safety Boundary

\boxed{E0, E1, E2 \not\Rightarrow E4}

without an independently validated inference mechanism.

H.3 Critical Correction

The correct mapping from evidence to hypotheses is:

\boxed{E2 \rightarrow \{H_1, H_2, \ldots, H_k\}}

not E2 \rightarrow H_1. The evidence supports multiple hypotheses, not a single concern.

